"represents": "Steady, practical success and generous friendship; the other version of the American Dream (as Bigsby suggests, built on hard work and charity rather than self-delusion).",
"relationships": "Willy is jealous of him and cannot take his help, yet he calls Charley his only friend. Charley's son Bernard is the opposite of Biff."
