"explanation": "Willy believes his affair in Boston ruined Biff's life, and the guilt keeps breaking into his mind. The Woman's laugh interrupts his present, and he cannot bear to see Linda mending stockings. Bigsby notes that the structure of the play reflects Willy's search for the moment when his life took a wrong turn. There is another betrayal in Willy's past: his father and his brother both left him. The family also betrays Willy: Happy and Biff leave him in the restaurant.",
