"explanation": "Ben's story is the opposite of Willy's life. Ben walked into the jungle and came out rich, and he keeps telling Willy there is opportunity in Alaska. Willy once nearly followed Ben, but he met Dave Singleman and chose to be a salesman instead. Willy cannot decide whether he made a mistake. The jungle story also suggests a harsh view of success: Ben says never to fight fair with a stranger. But the diamonds are not real for Willy, and the final \"diamond\" is his insurance money. The idea of a frontier also links to Biff, who loves outdoor work.",
