"timeline": [
"Willy comes home early from his sales trip because he cannot keep his mind on driving.",
"Biff and Happy talk in their old bedroom and plan to ask Bill Oliver for money for a ranch or a business.",
"Willy slips into memories of the boys, the car, and the laughter of The Woman.",
"Linda tells her sons that Willy has been trying to kill himself, and shows them the rubber hose.",
"Biff finds the rubber tubing behind the heater and takes it upstairs.",
"The next morning Willy is hopeful, but Howard fires him instead of giving him a New York job.",
"Willy borrows money from Charley and learns that Bernard will argue before the Supreme Court.",
"Biff waits all day for Oliver, who does not remember him, and Biff takes Oliver's fountain pen.",
"At the restaurant, Biff tries to tell the truth, and Willy remembers the Boston hotel room.",
"Willy hurries out to buy seeds, and Linda throws the roses on the floor and orders her sons out.",
"Willy plants seeds in the dark and talks with Ben about the insurance money.",
"Biff confronts Willy with the hose, tells the truth about himself, and cries in his arms.",
"Willy drives away in his car and dies.",
"At the funeral, few people come, and Linda says they are finally free."
],
